{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "sgp-dockermastery-content-delivery",
    "name": "SGP — Docker Mastery Content Delivery",
    "description": "End-to-end test suite for the content-delivery user story, scoped to the Docker Mastery course (courseId=docker-mastery, lab lab-1, module docker-fundamentals).\n\n⚠️ STALE (lab path changed): the backend proxy endpoints `/api/v1/labs/*`, `/api/v1/demos/*` and `WS /api/v1/labs/ws/lab` were REMOVED — the frontend talks to the orchestrator directly (`localhost:8001`, `Authorization: Bearer $ORCHESTRATOR_SECRET`, terminal `WS /ws/terminal`). Folders that exercise labs (A4–A6) 404 against the backend; run lab lifecycle against `orchestrator/postman_collection.json` (orchestrator direct) instead. Content handshake / catalog / progress folders (A1–A3, A7) remain valid.\n\nRUN ORDER: run folders 0 → 5 in order with the Collection Runner. Requests capture variables (version, sessionId, idToken, labConfigRaw, ...) consumed by later requests.\n\nAspects covered:\n  A1 Version handshake / content integrity (GET /api/v1/content/version)\n  A2 Client-side content delivery — backend serves NO content files; the frontend serves extracted local content (/api/local-content/*)\n  A3 Catalog + course TOC from Firestore (/api/v1/courses)\n  A4 Client-driven lab provisioning (env config in the start request body) — endpoint REMOVED; see stale note\n  A5 Client-driven task validation (task_type + validation in the validate request body) — endpoint REMOVED; see stale note\n  A6 Lab lifecycle proxy (start/tasks/validate/status/stop/resume/token/destroy) — REMOVED; use orchestrator/postman_collection.json\n  A7 Progress & completion in Firestore\n\nAUTH: protected endpoints use a Firebase ID token. Request 2.1 signs in with the Identity Toolkit REST API using {{firebaseApiKey}} + {{testEmail}}/{{testPassword}} and stores the token in {{idToken}}. Without Firebase config, folders 0–1 still pass (public); 2+ will 401.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{idToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "idToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "version",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "downloadUrl",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "artifactSha256",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "labConfigRaw",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "sessionId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "containerName",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0 · Content Bootstrap & Integrity",
      "description": "Aspect A1 + A2. Proves the version handshake (worker-persisted artifact_sha256 + derived download_url), that the frontend downloaded/verified/extracted the tarball, and — as a regression check — that the backend no longer serves content files.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "0.1 · GET /api/v1/content/version",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const data = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"version handshake shape\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(data).to.be.an('object');",
                  "  pm.expect(data.version).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(data.download_url).to.match(/^https?:\\/\\//);",
                  "  pm.expect(data.artifact_sha256).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('version', data.version);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('downloadUrl', data.download_url);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('artifactSha256', data.artifact_sha256);",
                  "",
                  "// Optional integrity probe: download_url must respond 200. Full",
                  "// sha256 verification is the frontend's job (ensureContent); this",
                  "// only proves the S3 URL is reachable from the client network.",
                  "pm.sendRequest({ url: data.download_url, method: 'GET' }, (err, res) => {",
                  "  pm.test(\"download_url reachable\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(err).to.not.exist;",
                  "    pm.expect(res.code).to.eql(200);",
                  "  });",
                  "  if (!err && res && res.code === 200 && res.body) {",
                  "    const hash = CryptoJS.SHA256(res.body).toString(CryptoJS.enc.Hex).slice(0, 16);",
                  "    console.log(`artifact sha256: expected=${data.artifact_sha256} got=${hash} match=${hash === data.artifact_sha256}`);",
                  "  }",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/content/version",
            "description": "A1 — The client bootstrap handshake. Must return {version, download_url, artifact_sha256} derived from Firestore contentVersion/artifact_sha256 + the configured public base URL. Backend performs no file reads."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "0.2 · GET /api/local-content/labs/{{courseId}}/{{labId}}/config",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const cfg = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"lab config resolves environment ref\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(cfg).to.be.an('object');",
                  "  pm.expect(cfg.lab_id).to.eql(pm.variables.get('labId'));",
                  "  pm.expect(cfg.environment).to.be.an('object');",
                  "  pm.expect(cfg.environment.base_image).to.eql('labops-docker:latest');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(\"config carries the tasks the client sends to start/tasks/validate\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(cfg.tasks).to.be.an('array').with.lengthOf.at.least(4);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('labConfigRaw', JSON.stringify(cfg));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{frontendUrl}}/api/local-content/labs/{{courseId}}/{{labId}}/config",
            "description": "A2 — Frontend serves the parsed lab.yaml from its extracted local content dir. The environment string ref (docker-basic) is resolved to an object here — this is exactly what the client sends in the start request body."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "0.3 · GET /api/local-content/labs/{{courseId}}/{{labId}}/instructions",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"instructions shape\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(d.lab_id).to.eql(pm.variables.get('labId'));",
                  "  pm.expect(d.title).to.eql('Hello World Container');",
                  "  pm.expect(d.module_id).to.eql('docker-fundamentals');",
                  "  pm.expect(d.instructions).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{frontendUrl}}/api/local-content/labs/{{courseId}}/{{labId}}/instructions",
            "description": "A2 — Lab instructions markdown served from local content (was: backend file route)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "0.4 · GET /api/local-content/labs/{{courseId}}/{{labId}}/tasks",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"local task list matches the lab spec\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(d.tasks).to.be.an('array');",
                  "  const ids = d.tasks.map(t => t.id);",
                  "  pm.expect(ids).to.include.members(['access-daemon','fix-group','count-images','run-simple-container']);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{frontendUrl}}/api/local-content/labs/{{courseId}}/{{labId}}/tasks",
            "description": "A2 — Task list read from local content. In the live flow the client sends this list to POST /api/v1/labs/.../tasks (A5)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "0.5 · GET /api/local-content/chapters/{{courseId}}/chapter-1",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"chapter markdown served from local content\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(d.content).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(d.content).to.match(/^#\\s/m);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{frontendUrl}}/api/local-content/chapters/{{courseId}}/chapter-1",
            "description": "A2 — Chapter markdown from the extracted tarball (was: backend file route)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "0.6 · REGRESSION — backend must NOT serve /api/v1/content/courses",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"old backend file routes are gone (expect 404)\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(404);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/content/courses",
            "description": "A2 regression — the old file-serving router was removed in branch 2. A 404 proves the backend no longer serves content; the catalog now comes from Firestore (/api/v1/courses)."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1 · Catalog & Course TOC (Firestore)",
      "description": "Aspect A3. Catalog and course structure are served from Firestore — the exact shape the worker derives from content-v2 (modules with ordered items/chapters/labs).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1.1 · GET /api/v1/courses",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const courses = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"catalog served from Firestore\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(courses).to.be.an('array');",
                  "  const dm = courses.find(c => c.id === pm.variables.get('courseId'));",
                  "  pm.expect(dm).to.exist;",
                  "  pm.expect(dm.title).to.eql('Docker Mastery');",
                  "  pm.expect(dm.level).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/courses",
            "description": "A3 — Course catalog (Firestore, seeded by the worker)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1.2 · GET /api/v1/courses/{{courseId}}",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const course = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"course TOC has docker-fundamentals with linear items\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(course.modules).to.be.an('array');",
                  "  const mod = course.modules.find(m => m.id === 'docker-fundamentals');",
                  "  pm.expect(mod).to.exist;",
                  "  const ids = mod.items.map(i => i.id);",
                  "  pm.expect(ids).to.eql(['chapter-1','chapter-2','lab-1','chapter-3','lab-2','lab-3']);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(\"content version metadata persisted by the worker\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(course.contentVersion).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(course.artifact_sha256).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/courses/{{courseId}}",
            "description": "A3 — Course TOC (Firestore). Also proves artifact_sha256/contentVersion were persisted by the worker (branch 2)."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2 · Auth & Enrollment",
      "description": "Prerequisite for all protected endpoints. 2.1 signs in with Firebase and stores the ID token; the collection-level bearer auth attaches it automatically.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "2.1 · Firebase sign-in (get ID token)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Firebase sign-in returns an ID token\", () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(d.idToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('idToken', d.idToken);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "auth": {
            "type": "noauth"
          },
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{testEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{testPassword}}\",\n  \"returnSecureToken\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": "https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1/accounts:signInWithPassword?key={{firebaseApiKey}}",
            "description": "Signs in via the Firebase Identity Toolkit REST API and saves {{idToken}}. Requires firebaseApiKey + a test user (email/password) in the environment."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.2 · POST /api/v1/users/sync",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"user synced\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(d.uid).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(d.enrolledCourses).to.be.an('array');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/sync",
            "description": "Creates/updates the user doc in Firestore from the verified Firebase token."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.3 · POST /api/v1/courses/{{courseId}}/enroll",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"enrolled\", () => {",
                  "  const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(d.status).to.eql('enrolled');",
                  "  pm.expect(d.courseId).to.eql(pm.variables.get('courseId'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/courses/{{courseId}}/enroll",
            "description": "Enrolls the user in docker-mastery and creates the enrollment progress doc."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2.4 · GET /api/v1/courses/{{courseId}}/progress",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"enrollment has progress state\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(d.courseId).to.eql(pm.variables.get('courseId'));",
                  "  pm.expect(d.progress).to.be.an('object');",
                  "  pm.expect(d.status).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/courses/{{courseId}}/progress",
            "description": "Baseline enrollment doc before any learning progress."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3 · Chapter Learning & Progress",
      "description": "Aspect A2 + A7. Read chapter content from the local content store, then persist chapter completion to Firestore.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "3.1 · GET /api/local-content/chapters/{{courseId}}/chapter-1",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"chapter markdown served from local content\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(d.content).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(d.content).to.match(/^#\\s/m);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{frontendUrl}}/api/local-content/chapters/{{courseId}}/chapter-1",
            "description": "A2 — Chapter markdown from the extracted tarball (was: backend file route)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3.2 · PUT /api/v1/courses/{{courseId}}/progress (mark chapter-1 complete)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"chapter marked complete\", () => {",
                  "  const p = pm.response.json().progress;",
                  "  pm.expect(p['docker-fundamentals']['chapter-1']).to.eql('completed');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"moduleId\": \"docker-fundamentals\",\n  \"chapterId\": \"chapter-1\",\n  \"status\": \"completed\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/courses/{{courseId}}/progress",
            "description": "A7 — Persist chapter completion to the Firestore enrollment doc."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4 · Lab Lifecycle (client-driven)",
      "description": "Aspects A4 + A5 + A6. The client owns the lab config: start carries the environment config, tasks carries the client task list, validate carries the per-task validation spec. The backend only proxies to the orchestrator. WARNING: 4.2 provisions a real Docker container on the host; 4.13 destroys it.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "4.1 · GET .../labs/{{labId}}/active",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (d && d.session_id) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('sessionId', d.session_id);",
                  "  console.log('Pre-existing session found:', d.session_id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/labs/courses/{{courseId}}/labs/{{labId}}/active",
            "description": "A6 — Read-through session check (orchestrator is the source of truth via Docker labels). Returns null when no live container."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4.2 · POST .../labs/{{labId}}/start (env config from client)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// The env config comes from the client's local lab config (0.2).",
                  "// This is the client-driven provisioning aspect (A4).",
                  "const raw = pm.variables.get('labConfigRaw');",
                  "const cfg = raw ? JSON.parse(raw) : null;",
                  "if (cfg) {",
                  "  const env = cfg.environment || {};",
                  "  pm.variables.set('startImage', env.base_image || '');",
                  "  pm.variables.set('startApt', JSON.stringify(env.apt_packages || []));",
                  "  pm.variables.set('startPrePull', JSON.stringify(env.pre_pull || []));",
                  "  pm.variables.set('startSetup', JSON.stringify(cfg.setup || []));",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.variables.set('startImage', 'labops-docker:latest');",
                  "  pm.variables.set('startApt', '[]');",
                  "  pm.variables.set('startPrePull', '[\"nginx:alpine\",\"alpine:latest\"]');",
                  "  pm.variables.set('startSetup', '[]');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"session provisioned\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(d.session_id).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(d.lab_id).to.eql(pm.variables.get('labId'));",
                  "  pm.expect(d.status).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(d.ws_token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(d.ws_url).to.match(/^wss?:\\/\\//);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('sessionId', d.session_id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('containerName', d.container_name);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"image\": \"{{startImage}}\",\n  \"apt_packages\": {{startApt}},\n  \"pre_pull\": {{startPrePull}},\n  \"setup\": {{startSetup}}\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/labs/courses/{{courseId}}/labs/{{labId}}/start",
            "description": "A4 — The client supplies {image, apt_packages, pre_pull, setup} taken from its resolved local config (0.2). The backend forwards to the orchestrator and returns a WebSocket session."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4.3 · GET .../labs/{{labId}}/status/{{sessionId}}",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"status reports the session\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(d.session_id).to.eql(pm.variables.get('sessionId'));",
                  "  pm.expect(d.status).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/labs/courses/{{courseId}}/labs/{{labId}}/status/{{sessionId}}",
            "description": "A6 — Proxy the container status from the orchestrator."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4.4 · POST .../labs/{{labId}}/tasks (task list from client)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// The task list comes from the client's local lab config (A5).",
                  "const raw = pm.variables.get('labConfigRaw');",
                  "const cfg = raw ? JSON.parse(raw) : null;",
                  "pm.variables.set('tasksJson', cfg && Array.isArray(cfg.tasks) ? JSON.stringify(cfg.tasks) : '[]');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"task list returned with options intact\", () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(d.tasks).to.be.an('array');",
                  "  pm.expect(d.tasks.map(t => t.id)).to.include('access-daemon');",
                  "  const count = d.tasks.find(t => t.id === 'count-images');",
                  "  pm.expect(count.options).to.eql(['1','2','3','4']);",
